   "In honour of Frank Duckworth (1939–2024)", 'Frank Duckworth was a British statistician. With Tony Lewis he created the Duckworth–Lewis method (1997), which fairly resets the target in cricket when rain interrupts a match: by the resources the team actually had, not by the full game. It later became the Duckworth–Lewis–Stern method. <a href="{wiki}" rel="noopener">' + W["en"] + '</a>.',
   "The sensor is named in his honour; Orb Studio is not connected with Frank Duckworth, his family or the Royal Statistical Society.", "Indices against the same time of day",
